==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-pay through the nose.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|pay<,,paid> through the nose}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To pay an [[exorbitant]] or [[excessive]] amount, either in [[money]] or in some other manner.
#: {{hyper|en|pay over the odds}}
#* '''1650''', George Walker, ''Anglo-Tyrannus,'' London: George Thompson, p.{{nbsp}}20,<sup>[http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A96861.0001.001]</sup>
#*: Observe here the happy estate of our Ancestors under Monarchy, who, if they gained but this advantage {{...}} of receiving a few good Grants, and enjoying a pittance of Freedom, once in 4 or 5 ages when their King was too young to play ''Rex,'' and there hapned a wise and honest Protector; yet were sure to '''pay through the nose''' for it afterwards with double and treble interest for forbearance.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1918|author=[[w:Peter_B._Kyne|Peter B. Kyne]]|title=The Valley of the Giants|chapter=36
|passage="You'll '''pay through the nose''' for this, you scoundrel," Sexton whimpered. "I'll fix you, you traitor."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1921|author=[[w:John_Galsworthy|John Galsworthy]]|title=The Forsyte Saga|section=part 2, ch. 4
|passage=That fellow would milk the settlements somehow, and make his family '''pay through the nose''' to keep him out of bankruptcy.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Brace for the Amazon effect on live sport|work=The Economist|date=2021-04-08|url=https://www.economist.com/business/2021/04/08/brace-for-the-amazon-effect-on-live-sport|issn=0013-0613|passage=At a time when other entertainment is available at a sliver of the price from Netflix and other streaming services, live sport is the only thing left to induce viewers to '''pay through the nose''' for pay-TV.}}

